  = conclusion: CLI parsing, transport, diagnostics, and exit mapping add no independent semantic resolution logic

& [AuthoritySeparation] is the local embedded runtime boundary
  + [semantic_request] carries caller identity, purpose, read-only boundary, requested scope, exact expected environment digest, expected package identities and digests, and query or inspect operation
  + [runtime_environment] separately carries operator-controlled trust roots, signed compiled packages, and trust time
  + [selection] is an explicit supervisor-pinned environment path rather than model-generated trust data inside the request
  + [substitution_gate] rejects any environment or package differing from request bindings before semantic lookup
  + [response_proof] returns observed environment digest, full admitted package set, and a core query-or-inspection result digest on success
  - never: allow request content to create or replace trust roots

& [ProtocolSolution] is the versioned machine surface
  + [protocol] is cantor-protocol/0.1
  + [environment] is cantor-embedded-environment/0.1
  + [query] is cantor-query/0.1
  + [commands] is query and inspect
  + [input] is UTF-8 JSON on standard input or explicit request file
  + [environment_input] is a separate explicit local file with a 64 MiB reader cap
  + [stdout] is exactly one compact JSON response plus one newline
  + [stderr] is diagnostics only
  + [strictness] is unknown protocol, environment, trust, package, query, and identity fields rejected rather than ignored

& [ExitClassSolution] is stable
  + [0] is success
  + [2] is invalid request
  + [3] is trust failure
  + [4] is unresolved semantic dependency
  + [5] is policy denial
  + [6] is semantic or proof fault
  + [70] is internal fault
  = must: preserve a structured JSON response for every handled nonzero class

& [CallerVerificationSolution] is fail-closed response use
  + [function] is verify_protocol_response
  + [checks] is request identity, operation, protocol, environment digest, admitted package set, package digests, status, exit, outcome, continuation, exact fault projection, core digest binding, recomputed core result digest, and selected package provenance
  + [stronger_function] is verify_protocol_response_against_environment
  + [stronger_check] is exact deterministic re-execution against the supervisor-pinned signed environment
  + [digest_boundary] is digest consistency is not response authentication when an attacker can replace both content and digest
  + [Codex_rule] is only a verified response may become reflection context
  + [fallback_rule] is nonzero exit or verification failure remains a visible fault and never permission to invent SOP

& [InspectableSurface] is read-only
  + [query] returns the exact core CantorQueryResult
  + [inspect_fabric] returns counts, signed source bytes, serialized package bytes, and package identities
  + [inspect_package] returns package proof plus unit and relation identities
  + [inspect_certificate] returns the recognition certificate
  + [inspect_semantic_unit] returns unit, package, certificate, signed source-document digest, and exact quote
  + [inspect_integrity] recomputably binds every typed inspect result to its protocol proof digest
  - never: mutate files, packages, trust, runtime state, or external effects

& [DeliberateLimitationSet] is retained
  + [trust_root_storage] is an operator-controlled local environment file; production key ceremony, ACL policy, HSM, and rotation remain outside this slice
  + [time_and_replay] is embedded trust time operator-supplied; production trusted-clock, freshness, revocation retention, and anti-rollback remain outside this slice
  + [caller_authentication] is outside this CLI; caller identity and scope are envelope declarations that a production supervisor must derive from authenticated ACL policy
  + [demo] is generated with public fixture keys and is never authority
  + [service] is no daemon, session store, cache, or network listener
  + [MCP] is not implemented or activated
  + [provider] is no Ollama, OpenAI, or other inference call
  + [effects] is read-only only
  - never: claim CEB-014 or CEB-015 from CLI evidence

